{"version":"1","id":"brackeys","handle":"brackeys","name":"Brackeys","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--aMECi2uY--/f_auto/v1717229850/logos/brackeys","description":null,"is_squad":false,"x":-7.0417,"y":-8.1147,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":57,"newest_post_at":"2026-01-18T21:00:45.000Z","oldest_post_at":"2019-07-21T20:00:00.000Z","features":{"hype_score":0.210526,"listicle_ratio":0.0,"question_ratio":0.035088,"avg_read_time":19.491228,"summary_length_avg":367.0,"title_length_avg":39.210526,"title_length_var":140.938135,"tag_entropy":2.406592,"tag_diversity":0.491228,"top_tag_share":0.035088,"avg_upvotes":2.666667,"median_upvotes":0.0,"avg_comments":0.087719,"comment_to_upvote_ratio":0.039216,"zero_engagement_share":0.578947,"viral_share":0.0,"posts_per_week":0.668847,"non_article_ratio":1.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"recency_skew":0.017857},"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[1.1471,0.8676],"cadence_depth":[-3.6176,8.6618],"hype_variety":[9.8676,-7.0735],"title_style":[3.9412,-2.4853]},"top_tags":[["unity",47],["c",36],["game-development",20],["course",19],["3d",9],["godot",8],["c#",5],["general-programming",4]],"sample_titles":{"representative":["How to program in Godot - GDScript Tutorial","How to make 3D Games in Godot","Best Games from the Brackeys Game Jam 2024.2!"],"outlier":["EVERY Image Effect in Unity Explained - Post Processing v2 Tutorial"]},"recent_posts":[{"id":"1INaRSjtp","title":"How to make VFX in Godot","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=htRjt505sPg","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/how-to-make-vfx-in-godot-1inarsjtp","summary":"A comprehensive guide to creating visual effects in Godot using particle systems. Covers GPU and CPU particles, process materials, billboarding techniques, blend modes, flipbook animations, and sub-emitters. Demonstrates building explosions, magic effects, fire, smoke, clouds, and rain through layered particle systems. Includes practical techniques like scale curves, color gradients, collision handling, and spawning effects via code. Provides free asset pack and custom plugin for particle preview workflow.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/htRjt505sPg/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-01-18T21:00:45.000Z"},{"id":"lt6mbEOXp","title":"Standout games from the 2025 Brackeys game jams","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1un4Tu2f-L4","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/best-games-from-the-brackeys-game-jam-2025--lt6mbeoxp","summary":"A showcase of standout games from the 2025 Brackeys Game Jams, where nearly 30,000 participants created 4,500 unique games. The review highlights creative interpretations of themes like \"nothing can go wrong\" and \"risk it for the biscuit,\" featuring innovative mechanics from platformers with movement restrictions to rhythm battlers and roguelike card games. Winners include Wrongfile, a multitasking game about fighting computer viruses on your first day at work, and Rave Cage Cyber Funk, a rhythm-based combat game with risk-reward mechanics.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/1un4Tu2f-L4/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":2,"created_at":"2025-10-05T20:00:02.000Z"},{"id":"lM5u4G0xt","title":"Lighting in Godot #gamedev #godot","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UR5TvKmeVhY","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/lighting-in-godot-gamedev-godot-lm5u4g0xt","summary":"A video tutorial covering lighting techniques in the Godot game engine, including global illumination, reflections, and light baking concepts to achieve different visual effects in games.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/UR5TvKmeVhY/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":3,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-06-11T10:25:39.000Z"},{"id":"C6PpFeddN","title":"Lighting in Godot for Beginners","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aRdiiWpA0AA","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/lighting-in-godot-for-beginners-c6ppfeddn","summary":"A comprehensive guide to lighting in Godot covering the fundamentals of 3D light nodes (directional, omni, spotlight), environment lighting, and emissive materials. Explores creative lighting techniques including three-point lighting, fog effects, and various global illumination methods (SDFGI, VoxelGI, lightmap baking). Demonstrates practical examples of lighting indoor tavern and outdoor daytime/nighttime scenes, with performance optimization tips and post-processing effects like glow and volumetric fog.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/aRdiiWpA0AA/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":7,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-06-08T20:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"YTDUNRA2x","title":"Understanding key components of 3D game assets","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MH38ZjNqv6g","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/3d-video-game-assets-in-1-minute-gamedev-tutorial-ytdunra2x","summary":"This post provides a one-minute overview of key components used in 3D video game development. It covers the mesh, UV maps for texturing, the creation of materials to simulate surface properties, and rigging for animation. The post explains how these elements are applied to create realistic and animated game assets.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/MH38ZjNqv6g/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":7,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-02-11T10:02:32.000Z"},{"id":"9UmUAIn19","title":"How to make 3D Games in Godot","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ke5KpqcoiIU","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/how-to-make-3d-games-in-godot-9umuain19","summary":"Learn how to transition from 2D to 3D game development using Godot. The video covers essential concepts such as using nodes, working with 3D assets, setting up basic functionalities and collisions, and managing physics. Additional topics include importing and configuring 3D models, adding animations, setting up lighting and environmental effects, and optimizing game performance. The guide aims to demystify 3D game development, making it accessible and manageable for both beginners and experienced developers.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/ke5KpqcoiIU/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":37,"num_comments":2,"created_at":"2025-02-09T21:00:32.000Z"},{"id":"rMdNGK9Q4","title":"Best Games from the Brackeys Game Jam 2024.2!","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2DSrk7WX7ho","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/best-games-from-the-brackeys-game-jam-2024-2--rmdngk9q4","summary":"The post discusses the highlights of the 12th Brackeys Game Jam where over 10,000 participants created numerous games. It features handpicked standout entries, detailing unique and diverse gameplay mechanics. The video also encourages viewer participation in future game jams and promotes Senma Academy's game development courses.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/2DSrk7WX7ho/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":27,"num_comments":1,"created_at":"2024-11-03T21:00:02.000Z"},{"id":"0PYXN0Jnn","title":"How to program in Godot - GDScript Tutorial","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=e1zJS31tr88","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/how-to-program-in-godot---gdscript-tutorial-0pyxn0jnn","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/e1zJS31tr88/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":40,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-05-12T20:00:09.000Z"},{"id":"3aPklTRz3","title":"How to make a Video Game - Godot Beginner Tutorial","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LOhfqjmasi0","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/how-to-make-a-video-game---godot-beginner-tutorial-3apkltrz3","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/LOhfqjmasi0/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":10,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-04-28T20:00:06.000Z"},{"id":"Ts4kiCcll","title":"The Future of Game Development","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EYt6uDr-PHQ","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/the-future-of-game-development-ts4kiccll","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/EYt6uDr-PHQ/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-04-21T20:00:08.000Z"}],"similar_handles":["t